  "question": {
    "text": "In a coil, the current changes from $-2 \\mathrm{~A}$ to $+2 \\mathrm{~A}$ in $0.2 \\mathrm{~s}$ and induces an emf of $0.1 \\mathrm{~V}$. The self inductance of the coil is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4NPuL",
      "text": "$4 \\mathrm{mH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GgR73",
      "text": "$1 \\mathrm{mH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NqeV3",
      "text": "$5 \\mathrm{mH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "j0sfG",
      "text": "$2.5 \\mathrm{mH}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$(E m f)_{\\text {induced }}=-L \\frac{d i}{d t}$<br />In magnitude form,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left|\\operatorname{Emf}_{\\text {ind }}\\right|=\\left|(-) L \\frac{\\mathrm{di}}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right| \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 0.1=\\frac{(\\mathrm{L})[+2-(-2)]}{0.2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{L}=\\frac{0.1 \\times 0.2}{4}=5 \\mathrm{mH}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
